# Shell scripts MUST be LF — they're consumed by bash inside Linux
# containers via Docker COPY. autocrlf=true on Windows dev boxes
# silently turns the shebang into `#!/bin/bash\r`, which the Linux
# kernel then fails to exec ("no such file or directory" for the
# interpreter, not the script). Enforce LF in the working tree.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Dockerfile + compose are read by Linux tooling — same risk.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
